{
  "note": "Hand-written (phase 5 design 4.4, 5.1, 5.3; D131, D132). What each act on a preset does, and what it refuses: the functions of packages/presets/src/rules.ts, which the admin routes refuse by (P1) and the installer and the platform data's check read. The reader is packages/presets/test/rules.test.ts; the phone does not read this file. Each function is called with a case's input (presetWriteEffect with the input as its one argument, reorderRanks(current, ordered), changedFixedFields(kind, before, after)) and must give `expected`. presetWriteEffect: act is create, edit, archive (Remove), restore, take_update, take_update_as_new or reorder (each flag reorderRanks moves); kind the preset's; state active or archived, null for a create; baseVersion the version the admin's form was loaded at (null for a create, a restore and a reorder, which take none), currentVersion the head's (null for a create); changedFixed and sameBody what the edit's body does against the current one; referencedBy the active presets that point at this one, counted by kind; archivedRefs how many archived presets the new body points at; nameTaken whether another active preset of the kind holds the name the act would give it; updateOnOffer whether platform_latest is above origin_version; updateChangesFixed whether the newest platform body changes a fixed field. It answers {refuse: code} or the head after the act: {stateAfter, versionAfter, customizedAfter}, and for take_update_as_new also `created`, the new preset. A stale base is any base other than the current version. Each act reads only what it needs, and refuses in this order, the first that holds: create: name_taken, reference_archived. edit: archived, stale, no_change, fixed_field, name_taken, reference_archived. archive: not_removable (the settings preset), archived, stale, referenced (any count above 0). restore: not_archived, name_taken, reference_archived. take_update: archived, stale, no_update, fixed_field, name_taken, reference_archived. take_update_as_new: not_removable, stale, no_update, referenced (only while the old one is active), name_taken (the new one's name, the old one's freed), reference_archived. reorder: archived. After the act: create, active at version 1, not customized; edit, active at the next version, customized; archive, archived at the same version, customized; restore, active at the same version, customized; take_update, active at the next version, not customized (origin_version becomes platform_latest); take_update_as_new, the old one archived at the same version and customized (its origin_key goes), the new one active at version 1, not customized; reorder, active at the next version, customized, since its rank is now the team's and a platform update must not put it back (PRD main 387). A flag patients carry is archived all the same (D131): patients are not presets. reorderRanks: current is the tier's active flags [{id, rank}], in any order; ordered the ids the admin put in order. Unless ordered holds every id of current exactly once and nothing else ({refuse: 'ids_mismatch'}), each flag's new rank is its place in ordered, counting from 1, times 10, and the answer lists, in ordered's order, the flags whose rank that changes. changedFixedFields: the fields fixed at creation that `after` changes from `before`, in this order: order_category behaviour; item unit, then result.type (no result is a type of its own, so gaining or losing a result changes it, which is why an item never moves into or out of a lab category); flag tier, then sensitive; field_supply_map noteTypeKey, then path (a map with no path differs from one with any); none for bundle, condition_supply_map, bag and settings. Bodies are made up.",
